Dynatrace One Agent Installation:
Register Trail version, then on apps install oneagent choose linux and follow the commands mentions there to install the agent on the server.

Infrastructure & Operations:
We can see here host infra statistics. It will show all the hosts where dynatrace is installed, we can choose any host and see the infra performace metrics of that host.
Inside we have many tabs
Overview - On overview it will show highlevel details of uptime, monitoring type like full stack or infrastructure etc, then availability, reachability, total logs for timeframe, events, SLOs. Then it will show CPU, memory, swap, availability, network traffic, system load, DNS queries , DNS errors etc. Then it will show the List of technologies that host currently handeling its availability, cpu, mem. Then list of connections, list of process in and porcess out ie incomming connection and outgoing connections. Then network(interface, bits received and send per sec) and Disk analysis(total disks, space available , used, , reads/sec, writes/sec, reads iops, writes iops etc) as well.
Info - Will have config about the host like no of core, mem, hypervisor type, ip,os name, version, arch, hostname
Processes -  process monitoring. Show top process cpu, memory, and its tech,  
REachability
Vulnerability - Show app vulnerability
Logs - Show all host logs inculde app logs as well
Events
SLOs
Connections
Whatever not mentioned above will read later on course.

Renaming the host:
Click on 3 dots, then setting->general setting - Rename. We can also revert old name using revert to old name option on same general settings place.

Tags:
Its a key value pair we can assign to all host, service and application etc. We can create manual and automatic tags.Manual tags need to do on each host manually, automatic tag, we can go create a condition based on that it will apply to all matching conditions.  
Same way like above we can create a tags for process groups as well.Click on process it will list all process, for those process you need to apply tags we can do it

Enable Maintenance Window:
Apps->Manage->Settings->General->Maintenance Windows- Set the maintenance window - Which will disable all the alerts during the maintenance window

Enable Process Availability Alerts:
Process availability in Dynatrace is a monitoring feature that tracks whether critical processes are running on your hosts and alerts you when they go offline or crash. eg Nginix , node etc
Apps->Manage->Settings->Analyze and alert->Alerts->Process availability

To Create Custom Alerts:
To create an custom alerts like cpu went above certain % send me alert or other alerts
Go to Apps->Manage->Settings->Analyze and alert->Alerts-All Alerts - Give DQL query - Then other conditions which is easy to read and create. Alerted alerts will shown in problems. To create a DQL, go to dashboard->Click + -> Explore Metrcis - >Get the data -> Choose DQL to convert to DQL and pasted the same DQL in Alerts DQL

Setup Synthetic Monitoring for Private Locations:
We need to install active gate on VM then only we can enable synthetci monitoring for provate location.In synthetci monitoring we can create our user flow using record flow using browser or using http method we can construct our own api and we can setup the frequency for monitoring default is 1min and it will continously monitor the performnce of those user flow with complete details, with req, resp, performance, alerts, failure etc
Go to fleet managment->Install->Synthetic Engine->Choose Deployment Type->Setu Token-> Create a Private Location(Complete the Setup of provate location that we need)-> Follow commands to install active gate on vm like setup one agent.
To create Synthetci monitoring for Flow or Api - Search - Syntetic->New Monitor->Browser or HTTP 
Choose Ondemend to check right away or Analyse execution to see the history with timeframes.

Using synthetic we can monitor the network connection using network availability using icmp, tcp and dns protacol. To read about what each dose refer Dynatarace in Chatgpt
